claimed: deploy-cloud-aws -- stage 3's first cloud (specs/deployment.md):
the `aws` target, Terraform for ECS Fargate.

AWS first because the backlog says so and it is right: ECS plus ALB
plus RDS plus ElastiCache plus EFS plus Secrets Manager exercises
every Need the model has.

The gate is the strongest one this arc has had: `terraform init` then
`terraform validate` in a container, which checks every resource type
and required argument against the AWS provider's own schema -- not a
parse, a semantic check. Live and docker-dependent.

The decision I expect to matter: a secret is NOT a Terraform resource,
because `terraform apply` writes its value into the state file in
plaintext. It is created out of band and read back by a data source,
the same shape as the cluster target's untemplated Secret and for a
sharper reason.

The boundary this target names: it uses the account's DEFAULT VPC and
does not build a network. Anything else is somebody's own module and
we are a declarative layer over what already exists.

Files: okay-deploy Aws.scala + Targets.scala, tests, specs, boards.
gcp and azure stay filed.
